      "evidence_refs": [
        {
          "source_id": "FISRC-c8567b52c3776e28",
          "quote": "&quot;Doctor-led longevity and preventive healthcare startup Vytalyou has raised Rs 9 crore in a pre-Series A round from Chetan Jain of Pharma Dose and Ratan Jain of Venus Industries at a valuation of around Rs 33 crore. The proceeds will be used to expand its network of Incremental Lifestyle Clinics in Mumbai, Vytalyou said in a press release. Founded in 2025 by Chirantan Bose and Preetesh Bhandari, Vytalyou provides preventive healthcare and longevity-focused services, combining diagnostics with personalised health interventions and medically supervised care. The Mumbai-based startup offers services across pathology, radiology, cardio-respiratory assessments, body composition evaluation, genetic and cancer screening, gut microbiome evaluation, personalised IV therapies and regenerative interventions. It also offers non-invasive pain management technologies for chronic musculoskeletal conditions. Vytalyou uses an AI-based algorithm for its Predictive Longevity Evaluation, which assesses an individual&amp;quot;s health profile, biological ageing and potential health risks. Doctors review the assessment and develop a medically supervised care plan based on the findings. The company said it has served close to 1,000 clients since opening its first centre, with around half coming through walk-ins and the rest through word-of-mouth referrals. It plans to expand to 10 locations across India in the coming years. Vytalyou operates in India&amp;quot;s growing preventive healthcare and longevity segment, which has also seen startups such as Biopeak, Cent, Elevate Now and Decode Age raise capital. Biopeak raised $2.7 million in follow-on funding in January this year, while Cent, co-founded by Practo&amp;quot;s Shashank ND, raised around $5 million for its AI-led early-detection platform covering cancer, cardiac, neurological and metabolic risks. Elevate Now raised Rs 18 crore in a seed round, while Decode Age raised Rs 14.48 crore in a pre-Series A round to expand its longevity research, biomarker discovery, multi-omics and microbiome capabilities. &quot;",
          "source_content_hash": "5774882366d2c4f5746c8ae784bb63e142a0c621e5468f9ad8dda965d9020199",
          "quote_hash": "5774882366d2c4f5746c8ae784bb63e142a0c621e5468f9ad8dda965d9020199"
        },
